 "recap": [
  "Possession puts the thing first and the owner second: ang bahay ni Ana.",
  "Ni (one name), nina (two or more names), ng (common noun), ng mga (more than one).",
  "Possessive pronouns have a before-form (aking, iyong, kaniyang, aming, ating, inyong, kanilang) and an after-form (ko, mo, niya, namin, natin, ninyo, nila).",
  "Avoid repeating the same form twice. Mix one before-form and one after-form.",
  "With plurals, the possessive goes between ang and mga.",
  "Nito, niyan and niyon show the owner of this or that, and always go after the noun."
 ]
